{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 56, :comments ["And for a bright spot — the heh, alef, het, heh, ayin cause the word to change at the etnaḥta and the end of the verse. From בַּהֶרֶת to בֶּהָרֶת. The live goat (הַחַי), at the etnaḥta: the live goat (הֶחָי). So and so shall you eat (הֶחָרֶב). And they shall wash their clothes (וְהִטָּהָרוּ) without an etnaḥta."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The Hebrew acronym ה\"י א\"ח ה\"ע is expanded here as the letters heh, alef, het, heh, ayin based on context: Rashbam lists consonants whose presence causes vowel changes; the specific phonological principle is inferred from the examples given."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:49.876542588Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}